{
  "version": "schemaxis.readiness/1",
  "routes": {
    "schemaxis.ngspice/1": {
      "guide": "docs/ngspice.md",
      "context": {
        "purpose": "Simulate declared ideal linear circuits and publish verified numeric tables: DC resistor/capacitor sweeps, AC resistor/capacitor/inductor frequency response and one first-order RC step response. Optional named finite-sample voltage or AC gain acceptance determines whether the verified circuit meets the intended performance.",
        "assumptions": "Qualified ngspice-47 executable in an isolated process with startup files disabled. SI volts, ohms, farads, henries, Hz and seconds. One ideal voltage source to ground node 0. AC phasors use exp(+j*omega*t).",
        "constraints": "At most sixteen non-ground nodes, 64 resistors, 64 capacitors, 64 AC-only uncoupled inductors and 512 samples. Every node needs a resistor/inductor path to ground or the driven node. No ideal-inductor loops or inductive shorts across the source. No arbitrary netlists, models, semiconductors, mutual coupling, imported KiCad projects, inductor DC sweeps or general transient networks. rcStep is exactly series R and shunt C, initially uncharged, over 0.01\u201320 RC time constants. AC requires at least three points and at most fifteen selected probes within the shared 64-column table limit. Every requested frequency must have a nonsingular, sufficiently conditioned nodal system. Requirements inspect declared samples only; no continuous operating-envelope or all-component-tolerance guarantee. Phase acceptance is unsupported.",
        "inspection": "Inspect results.csv for selected voltages and AC real/imaginary/magnitude/phase columns. circuit-summary.json retains topology, units, first/last sample and independent maximum voltage discrepancy. circuit.cir is the generated inspectable netlist. Named requirements retain minimum/maximum native observations, signed bound margins and worst sample coordinates.",
        "recovery": "FLOATING_CIRCUIT needs a resistor/inductor reference path. INVALID_SWEEP needs stop > start. ILL_CONDITIONED_CIRCUIT needs damping or bounded component ratios. UNSUPPORTED_CIRCUIT requires the first-order RC topology for rcStep or removal of an ideal-inductor/source loop for AC. Configure ngspice-47 for INTERPRETER_NOT_FOUND; retain native logs and correct the input before a fresh attempt. INVALID_REQUIREMENT needs a supported quantity/probe and an ordered sample-containing window. PERFORMANCE_NOT_MET needs review of the worst condition, circuit/excitation or authored bounds, then a fresh attempt; this is distinct from native/physics failure."
      },
